Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Build a Large Language Model from Scratch \[LongDash] in Wolfram Language\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"695c24c3-a4fb-4b3a-85c2-d47cae9d2582"],

Cell["Part 6: Supervised fine-tuning (instruction following)", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"1fe8f2ed-30f4-40e0-ba22-feebe83fd3b1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The model after Part 4 can continue Shakespeare \[LongDash] but it has ",
 "no concept of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]a user asks a question, an assistant \
answers\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. ",
 "Supervised fine-tuning teaches that concept by training the same ",
 "next-token loss on a dataset where the inputs are already formatted ",
 "in the chat template ",
 StyleBox["<|user|>...<|assistant|>...<|eot|>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ". The same ",
 StyleBox["NetTrain",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " call we used in Part 4, on different data."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"693a7c5a-efe8-43a9-b8b0-0e560454ed45"],

Cell["1.  Setup and chat-format vocabulary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"87de9c7f-c89b-4268-a203-9d7f707e8724"],

Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0c52bdf6-b617-4e95-b20a-c51d170ba70e"],

Cell["\<\
Get[\"../../part-01-tokeniser-and-embeddings/src/Tokeniser.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-02-self-attention/src/Attention.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-03-transformer-block/src/Transformer.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-04-pretraining/src/Training.wl\"]
Get[\"src/SFT.wl\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"963e8bab-735b-4692-85c9-f68b33abbc62"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We add three special tokens to the BPE vocabulary, after the BPE ",
 "merges learned in Part 1: ",
 StyleBox["<|user|>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["<|assistant|>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["<|eot|>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ". Their IDs land at the end of the embedding matrix; the rest of the ",
 "vocabulary keeps its pretrained rows."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7de0251c-cb1e-465d-a396-384f7a34e094"],

Cell["\<\
bpe = Import[\"../../part-01-tokeniser-and-embeddings/data/bpe_trained.mx\"];
baseVocab = LLMAtoZ`Tokeniser`buildBPEVocabulary[bpe];
chatVocab = LLMAtoZ`SFT`extendVocabulary[baseVocab];
tokId = AssociationThread[chatVocab -> Range[Length[chatVocab]]];
{Length[baseVocab], Length[chatVocab]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"248bbd97-74fd-4b35-ba76-8c81eb27343a"],

Cell["2.  The chat template", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9b36f43b-3adf-48c5-bb5f-aca2257b1a87"],

Cell["\<\
Every turn in the training data is formatted into a single string with the \
special tokens marking role boundaries:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"622a5395-9d54-4997-9df1-d8db492f5400"],

Cell["\<\
LLMAtoZ`SFT`formatConversation[\"What is a sonnet?\",
  \"A sonnet is a poem of fourteen lines.\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"53321c59-347f-4b2b-b545-715f6cbe76e1"],

Cell["\<\
row = LLMAtoZ`SFT`tokeniseConversation[\"What is a sonnet?\",
  \"A sonnet is a poem of fourteen lines.\", bpe[\"MergeRules\"], tokId];
{Length[row[\"ids\"]], Total[row[\"assistantMask\"]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"65859d17-eedd-4e8a-aca9-97ceaae4bf3e"],

Cell["3.  The toy instruction dataset", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9e07d8d2-9d51-42e1-bade-64e97e898c70"],

Cell["\<\
Twenty hand-written Shakespeare-themed {user, assistant} pairs ship with the \
package. Just enough to demonstrate SFT end to end on the Mac mini; the same \
code consumes the SmolTalk subset when scaled up via the cloud path.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e1957c6-e4de-46ea-8f27-af2b7d63e161"],

Cell["LLMAtoZ`SFT`toyInstructionDataset[][[1 ;; 4]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c38b4be4-9b47-4fab-9a89-4904c05f3788"],

Cell["4.  Expand the model and train", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4686f59e-56ee-42d5-b592-82cee301baa8"],

Cell["\<\
Load the pretrained model from Part 4, expand its token-embedding and output \
projection to the new chat vocab size (adding random rows for the three \
special tokens), then run a short SFT pass.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"33d40ece-7c89-492a-ba96-6ab98a8c37c5"],

Cell["\<\
pretrained = Import[
  \"../../part-04-pretraining/data/tiny_gpt_trained.wlnet\"];
expanded = LLMAtoZ`SFT`expandModelVocabulary[pretrained, Length[chatVocab]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"84018241-6eee-440d-bcb3-df0d6c1f3533"],

Cell["\<\
dataset = LLMAtoZ`SFT`prepareSftDataset[
  LLMAtoZ`SFT`toyInstructionDataset[],
  bpe[\"MergeRules\"], tokId, 64];
Length[dataset]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c002849c-8ce2-485d-b0e2-5d8214f12a22"],

Cell["\<\
sftResult = LLMAtoZ`SFT`trainSft[expanded, dataset,
  <|\"BaseLR\" -> 0.0005, \"MaxRounds\" -> 8, \"BatchSize\" -> 4|>];
{sftResult[\"FinalLoss\"], sftResult[\"WallSeconds\"]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ba34f697-a941-4304-aec1-5cb27a1bda4c"],

Cell["5.  Generate a response", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ae5ead56-8bdf-42c1-92d9-1ab3923ae2ce"],

Cell["\<\
Same sampling code as in Part 5, but the model now produces text in the SFT \
chat template, so we stop at <|eot|>.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b88cd3d4-bc5a-4993-a40f-593524174f22"],

Cell["\<\
sftSample[net_, q_String, T_:0.8] := Module[
  {ids, ctx, pos, logits, p, sampled, contextLen = 64,
   eotId = tokId[\"<|eot|>\"],
   idTok = AssociationThread[Range[Length[chatVocab]] -> chatVocab]},
  ids = Lookup[tokId,
    LLMAtoZ`Tokeniser`bpeEncode[
      \"<|user|>\" <> q <> \"<|assistant|>\", bpe[\"MergeRules\"]]];
  (* fall back via lookup loop *)
  Do[
    ctx = If[Length[ids] >= contextLen, ids[[-contextLen ;;]],
              PadRight[ids, contextLen, 1]];
    pos = Min[Length[ids], contextLen];
    logits = net[ctx][[pos]];
    p = Exp[(logits - Max[logits])/T]; p = p/Total[p];
    sampled = RandomChoice[p -> Range[Length[p]]];
    AppendTo[ids, sampled];
    If[sampled === eotId, Break[]],
    {60}];
  StringReplace[StringJoin @ Lookup[idTok, ids],
    {\"</w>\" -> \" \", \"<|user|>\" -> \"\\nUSER: \",
     \"<|assistant|>\" -> \"\\nASSISTANT: \", \"<|eot|>\" -> \"\"}]
];
sftSample[sftResult[\"Net\"], \"What is a sonnet?\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"369b702b-dcba-4ae7-b96b-f2d990a0a8bd"],

Cell["6.  Parameter-efficient SFT with LoRA", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dac5fd5e-26e5-4011-9451-14a54d080204"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Full SFT updates every weight in the pretrained model. ",
 StyleBox["LoRA",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (Hu et al. 2021) updates a tiny fraction. The trick: for each ",
 "linear layer with weight ",
 Cell[BoxData["W"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"635dbcbb-9ea0-45ff-b4cb-d364ab942203"],
 " of shape ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["d", "in"], "\[Times]", 
   SubscriptBox["d", "out"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"764f6dcc-c4be-48e7-9ece-17c0e2cda9b3"],
 ", freeze ",
 Cell[BoxData["W"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"47e40a59-644c-408b-9e49-856783a779af"],
 " and learn two small matrices ",
 Cell[BoxData["A"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"bc53e6cd-6c67-4ecf-ae06-c77347c72c9b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["B"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"82420381-a66b-4750-bce5-2ef484819615"],
 " of ranks ",
 Cell[BoxData["r"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"704a928f-820d-441d-a8d0-d177c90e61eb"],
 " so the effective weight at inference is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"W", "+", "BA"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"1bfe8b12-de1b-45ed-8ee8-17660062c23a"],
 ". For r = 8 and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", "768"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"c9d5a130-04b9-4a7e-96f1-2a7169cd722f"],
 ", LoRA adds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"8", "\[Times]", "(", "768", "+", "768", ")", "=", "12288"}]], 
  "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"2cf8519d-cc3f-4ad4-aa25-7205f7522ed2"],
 " parameters versus the full ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"768", "\[Times]", "768"}], " ", "=", " ", "589"}], ",", "824"}]],
   "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"dcf887b0-d2c1-463b-9690-1138ec1269ac"],
 " \[LongDash] a 48\[Times] reduction."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b76f4c6-dbc7-4ee4-92d4-ee5b54cc2ffa"],

Cell["Get[\"src/Lora.wl\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b7e7da3e-7a1a-49c0-91da-1a5885bbebb7"],

Cell["\<\
(* Build a small LoRA delta and confirm zero-init identity. *)
delta = LLMAtoZ`Lora`loraDelta[64, 64, 8];
Print[\"loraDelta params: \", Information[delta, \"ArraysTotalElementCount\"]];
Print[\"vs full LinearLayer params: \", 64*64]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4ca7c23c-d1dd-4c54-8623-887e23c30f43"],

Cell["\<\
LLMAtoZ`Lora`loraParameterCount[768, 768, #] & /@ {4, 8, 16, 32, 64}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"60668125-e520-4733-a931-6bdd74671a00"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compare to the full per-attention-block parameter count of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    SubscriptBox["d", "model"], "2"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"7cc4421b-1635-4f16-9ea5-d600525a8fd8"],
 " = 4\[Times]768\[Times]768 \[TildeEqual] 2.36M parameters: even ",
 "rank-64 LoRA on all four QKV+output projections costs only ",
 "~100K parameters per layer, a >20\[Times] saving. With 12 layers ",
 "that is ~1.2M trainable LoRA parameters vs ~28M in full SFT."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06da4d86-eddf-400a-ac2d-3a67e2c3c566"],

Cell[BoxData[
 $CellContext`subsection["6.1  Interactive: choose your LoRA rank"]], "Input",\
ExpressionUUID->"bf094817-bd33-4a9f-b718-fad8156a2d69"],

Cell["\<\
Manipulate[
  With[{loraPer = LLMAtoZ`Lora`loraParameterCount[768, 768, r],
        fullPer = 768*768},
    Column[{
      Style[Row[{\"LoRA params per linear: \", loraPer}], 14, Bold],
      Style[Row[{\"Full linear params:     \", fullPer}], 12],
      Style[Row[{\"Savings: \",
        NumberForm[100. (1 - loraPer/fullPer), 4], \"%\"}], 12, Gray]
    }]
  ],
  {{r, 8, \"LoRA rank\"}, 1, 128, 1, Appearance -> \"Labeled\"},
  ControlPlacement -> Top]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dc9ea766-d97b-48a1-9e54-deb000bd659b"],

Cell["7.  Classification fine-tuning (Raschka chapter 6)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e4c2690b-cdec-453a-94bd-17fece1b4820"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Same pretrained model, very different task: ",
 StyleBox["classification.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " Instead of producing the next token, output a single ",
 "class label given the whole sequence. The architectural change is ",
 "tiny: strip the LM head (per-position vocab projection), add a ",
 StyleBox["SequenceLastLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " to pool the hidden state at the final position, then a fresh ",
 StyleBox["LinearLayer[nClasses]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ". The rest of the model \[LongDash] all the pretrained ",
 "transformer blocks \[LongDash] is reused as-is."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"08a801de-2b75-4fb3-b3f1-8ec8fd3dda3e"],

Cell["Get[\"src/Classification.wl\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"307c5546-ccb9-4df0-8a3d-4c1a5921ffc6"],

Cell["\<\
classifier = LLMAtoZ`Classification`attachClassifier[
  pretrained, 2, 96];
classifier\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"55eb5d57-a101-4837-a1f2-ca8585cf2fc1"],

Cell["\<\
Demo task: classify Shakespeare excerpts as tragedy (1) or comedy (2). The \
package ships a 20-pair hand-curated dataset for the demo; the same code \
consumes IMDb-sentiment or AG News if you supply them.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b6d388f-537c-403d-bc82-c67097f977e5"],

Cell["\<\
clsData = LLMAtoZ`Classification`prepareClassificationDataset[
  LLMAtoZ`Classification`shakespeareGenreLabels[],
  bpe[\"MergeRules\"], tokId, 64];
Length[clsData]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9763d913-b300-45b6-aba5-4a31b82bc3b6"],

Cell["\<\
clsResult = LLMAtoZ`Classification`trainClassifier[
  classifier, clsData,
  <|\"BaseLR\" -> 0.001, \"MaxRounds\" -> 6, \"BatchSize\" -> 4|>];
{clsResult[\"FinalLoss\"], clsResult[\"WallSeconds\"]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"522ba51a-0035-4bb8-9ad6-4a2f3b1676ee"],

Cell["\<\
LLMAtoZ`Classification`classifySample[clsResult[\"Net\"],
  LLMAtoZ`Classification`prepareClassificationDataset[
    {{\"To be, or not to be, that is the question.\", 0}},
    bpe[\"MergeRules\"], tokId, 64][[1, \"Input\"]]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a5f6cbfc-eecb-4b6d-9a85-a02ff479d86e"],

Cell["\<\
Caveat: with only 20 training examples and a tiny base model, the classifier \
will overfit and barely generalise. The mechanics are exactly right; scale \
the dataset to thousands of examples (and the model to 25M+ params) and the \
same code path produces a working spam/sentiment/topic classifier. Raschka's \
chapter 6 uses ~5K samples for the same target.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10162401-afa4-4bf4-809a-6e5ffe8bfde2"],

Cell["8.  Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"82d6bb34-f575-4629-b5cd-0ccd7733f7cb"],

Cell["\<\
Part 6 covers the three main fine-tuning regimes that turn a pretrained \
next-token model into something useful:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2be529b8-ba83-4ba9-beff-61bcf17924ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[FilledSquare] ",
 StyleBox["Full SFT for instruction following.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Chat template, vocab extension, ",
 StyleBox["expandModelVocabulary",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " for grafting new rows onto the pretrained embedder and output ",
 "projection.\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] ",
 StyleBox["LoRA for parameter-efficient SFT.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ",
 StyleBox["loraDelta",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["loraWrap",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["applyLoraToLinear",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["trainLora",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " \[LongDash] 20-50\[Times] fewer trainable parameters than full SFT, ",
 "no degradation in result quality at the scales most users actually ",
 "run.\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] ",
 StyleBox["Classification fine-tuning.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Strip the LM head, pool the last-position hidden state, project ",
 "to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "classes"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"8b38bafd-48dd-4fc4-ae87-dfb33547e52c"],
 " logits. Same pretrained backbone; entirely different output ",
 "objective. The Raschka chapter-6 setup."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"051ff1a5-5ea6-4278-b8ac-c9166c86dc9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In ",
 StyleBox["Part 7",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " we go beyond imitation and apply ",
 StyleBox["reinforcement learning",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " on top of the SFT model: GRPO with a verifiable binary reward, ",
 "no separate reward model, the recipe from nanochat."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2975563a-1c73-4d31-a113-f4cd7eab6ea3"]
},
